Hi,

=A0 I have a LSI 3801E PCIe SAS HBA based on the LSI 1068E controller conne=
cted to 8 SATA hot swap drive bays running under Fedora 11 X86_64 (2.6.29.4=
-167.fc11).=A0 I have 4 SATA drives hanging off of each external (4 SAS cha=
nnels) connector.=A0 I am having the following issue.=A0 If I have 2+ drive=
s on the same connect and replace one drive, when the new drive is detected=
, it resets all drives on the connector.=A0 So any drive that was mounted g=
oes offline.

For example:

/dev/sde1 - mounted to /media/disk1
/dev/sdf, /dev/sdg, /dev/sdh - 3 other drives connected to the same SAS con=
nector.

I removed sdh and reinserted it.=A0 When the drive is discovered and given =
a device entry, /dev/sde gets some sort of reset that makes the /media/disk=
1 mount fail and is no longer available.=A0 I've posted a copy of the kerne=
l messages when this happened.

Is this a driver issue, a configuration issue, or is it just how the 1068E =
works and there is no way around it?

Thanks!

